    <DataNode elementId="AT1G65060-MONOMER" textLabel="4-coumarate--CoA ligase 3" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9S777" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="535" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">4-coumarate coenzyme A ligase is encoded by a gene family of three members, &lt;i&gt;4CL1&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;4CL2&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;4CL3&lt;/i&gt;. The 4CL1, 4CL2 and 4CL3 proteins were expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; where they were shown to have different substrate specificities. 4CL1 has higher substrate specificity for 4-coumarate and caffeate than ferulate. 4CL2 has higher specificity for caffeate than coumarate, and ferulate is not a substrate of 4CL2. 4CL3 has higher specificity for 4-coumarate than caffeate and ferulate. All three proteins are also able to convert cinnamate, albeit with low efficiency, and none would convert sinapate.</Comment>
