    <DataNode elementId="AT1G62940-MONOMER" textLabel="AT1G62940-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9LQ12" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="695" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">ACOS5 (AT1G62940) is an acyl-CoA synthase and is preferentially expressed in the flowers. It is proposed to be involved in sporopollenin monomer biosynthesis. ACOS5 mutant produced no pollen in mature anthers. Pollen wall formation was severely compromised with an apparently lack of sporopollenin. In vitro enzyme assay of the recombinant protein indicated broad substrate specificity for medium- to long-chain fatty acids, with a preference for substituted fatty acids carrying a hydroxyl group at position C8 to C16 |CITS: [19218397]|.</Comment>
